# Java comments

Write comments in English, directly in the source file. If an applicable `AGENTS.md` (the project root, or a closer one in a parent directory of the file) sets a different comment language, follow that language instead. Do not add scripts, generators, or bulk-edit tooling whose purpose is to create or update comments.

## Javadoc

Add a 1–2 line Javadoc on every class, field, and method that is not covered by OpenAPI annotations below. Skip injected bean fields in services and controllers, as described under Injected beans.

```java
/** Loads a user by id and returns the public profile. */
public UserProfile loadProfile(UUID id) { ... }

/** Stable identifier of the user. */
private final UUID id;
```

## OpenAPI instead of Javadoc

When the project uses Swagger OpenAPI (`io.swagger.v3.oas.annotations`):

- Document controllers and their methods with `@Tag`, `@Operation`, `@Parameter`, `@ApiResponse`, and related annotations. Do not add Javadoc on those types and methods.
- If a class appears in OpenAPI Schemas, document its informational fields with `@Schema`. Do not add Javadoc on those fields.

Keep Javadoc on types and members that are not part of the OpenAPI surface.

```java
@Tag(name = "Users", description = "Read and update user profiles.")
@RestController
public class UserController {

    @Operation(summary = "Returns the public profile for a user id.")
    @ApiResponse(responseCode = "200", description = "Profile found.")
    @GetMapping("/users/{id}")
    public UserProfile get(@Parameter(description = "User id.") @PathVariable UUID id) { ... }
}

@Schema(name = "UserProfile")
public class UserProfile {

    @Schema(description = "Stable identifier of the user.")
    private UUID id;
}
```

## Injected beans

Do not add a comment on a field of a service or controller when that field is an injected bean (constructor injection, `@Autowired`, `@Inject`, or an equivalent container-managed dependency).

If such a field already has a comment, leave it. Do not remove or rewrite it only because the field is an injected bean.

```java
@Service
public class UserService {

    private final UserRepository users;

    public UserService(UserRepository users) {
        this.users = users;
    }
}
```

## When code changes

After changing a class, method, or field, re-read the comments on the types you touched and update any that no longer match the code.

## Inline comments

If a method’s logic is hard to follow, add short `//` comments at the non-obvious steps. Do not restate what the code already says.

```java
// Retry only transient timeouts; a 4xx is a permanent client error.
if (status >= 500) {
    return backoff(attempt);
}
```
